  "title": "Confirmation of Co-operation and Representation",
  "sourceSha256": "d6f07c5ea13c20d6935e7162b8206841d2c40c7f88ffe137c64d55827c92cdf8",
  "note": "Curation for Form 320. One entry per blank id emitted by tools/extract_template.py. The form calls the listing side the 'Seller Brokerage'; it is the same party Form 100 calls the listing brokerage, so the blanks reuse those names rather than inventing a second set for one value.",
  "kinds": {
    "data": "Filled before signing. The compliance gate checks these unless they are marked optional.",
    "signature": "Drawn by a signer in the e-sign session. Never filled by us.",
    "signingDate": "Dated by the signer at execution, not by the agent."
  },
  "sections": {
    "required": "The two brokerages and the deal they are confirming. All nine come from the domain model or the agent's profile — 320 asks for almost nothing that Form 100 has not already been told.",
    "declarations": "Sections 1 to 4 are numbered alternatives with tick boxes the extractor cannot see, and their comment lines are alternatives to each other: section 4b) offers either the MLS commission amount OR a free-text description of how the co-operating brokerage is paid. Requiring either would make the other unfillable, so the whole block is optional.",
    "addresses": "The two unlabelled lines under each brokerage's name. The form prints no caption for them and the second sits below the Tel/Fax row, so they are treated as an address block rather than guessed at more precisely — and left optional for the same reason. Deliberately no `flow`: a second address line is a city and postal code, not the overflow of the first."
  },
